meta {
  name: live sessions
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/sessions/live
  body: none
  auth: none
}

docs {
  Which sessions are live on this server right now: one row per live session ({id, running, since}), oldest claim first. The polled floor under the live_sessions socket push — an empty list is a fact, not an error.
  
  Fence: host — Loopback fence: the TCP peer must be loopback AND the Host header must be localhost/127.0.0.1/::1. A REST client passes automatically when it targets http://localhost:<port>. A LAN IP or rebound DNS name in the URL answers a blank 404.
  
  Writes state: no
}
